<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1818" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Algĭdus</span></b> , i,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				high snow-capped mountain</i>, <i>and the forest
				upon it</i>, <i>south-east of Rome</i>, <i>between Tusculum and Velitrœ</i>, now <i>Monte Compatri</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 26,
				9, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 13, 34, § 130</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gelidus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 21, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nivalis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 23, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				C. S. 69</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Algĭdum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>a town upon
			it</i>, now <i>Pava</i>, <i><span class="en">Flor. 1,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Algĭdus</span></b> , a, um, <i>pertaining to Algidum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					6, 722</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secessus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					10, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
